Suleimani Balochi ↔ English (Apertium language-pair prototype)
===============================================================================

This repository is intended to become a bidirectional Apertium language pair
for Suleimani Balochi and English:

* Balochi → English (bal-eng)
* English → Balochi (eng-bal)

## Important development status

The repository currently contains a Kurdish (Northern Kurdish/Kurmanji, `kmr`)
Apertium scaffold and linguistic resources. The repository name and its
description do not make those resources Balochi. In particular, the existing
bilingual dictionary, transfer rules, test fixtures, and mode definitions must
not be presented as a working Balochi translator.

This first migration step establishes the target language identity and
documents the work still required. Until Balochi monolingual data and
Balochi-specific bilingual resources have been integrated and tested, this
package is a development prototype, not a functional Suleimani Balochi
translation system.

## Target language profile

* Language: Balochi (`bal`, ISO 639-3)
* Variety: Suleimani Balochi, as specified and reviewed by native speakers
* Target directions: `bal-eng` and `eng-bal`
* Initial orthography: to be agreed with native speakers before dictionary
  entries and morphological paradigms are committed

The dialect label "Suleimani" must be treated as a linguistic requirement,
not as a synonym for Kurdish Sulaymaniyah/Sorani or Kurmanji. Do not import
Kurdish vocabulary, morphology, or grammatical rules as Balochi data.

## Migration plan

1. Establish and document the Suleimani Balochi dialect and spelling
   conventions with native-speaker review.
2. Add or develop a Balochi monolingual Apertium package (`apertium-bal`):
   lexical categories, morphological paradigms, analyzer/generator,
   disambiguation, and tests.
3. Replace the Kurdish bilingual dictionary with reviewed Balochi–English
   lexical entries and explicit part-of-speech/semantic mappings.
4. Rewrite both translation directions' transfer, lexical-selection,
   interchunk, and postchunk rules for Balochi grammar and English.
5. Replace Kurdish corpora, tagger models, test fixtures, and documentation
   with Balochi material.
6. Update build dependencies, package metadata, modes, and installation paths
   to `bal-eng` / `eng-bal`; validate and run both directions end-to-end.

See [docs/SULEIMANI-BALOCHI-DESIGN.md](docs/SULEIMANI-BALOCHI-DESIGN.md)
for the initial linguistic and engineering checklist.

## Build status

The current build configuration still refers to the legacy `kmr` scaffold.
It is intentionally not advertised as a Balochi build yet: switching only
package labels or mode names would produce a misleading or broken translator.
The build configuration will be migrated together with the corresponding
Balochi lexical and morphological resources.

## Apertium

Apertium is a free/open-source rule-based machine-translation platform.
For general information and installation instructions, see
https://apertium.org/ and https://wiki.apertium.org/wiki/Installation.

